<data name="PolicyHelp" xml:space="preserve"><value>Thresholds compare estimated cost with total labor, vendor charges and committed parts. Unknown costs or currencies without a rule require review. Approvals are independent and currency-specific.</value></data>
<data name="BusinessCalendarHelp" xml:space="preserve"><value>Choose local working days and hours; 00:00 as the end means midnight. Enter holidays one per line. Set both targets to zero to disable a priority. Deadlines start at creation; priority edits recalculate them. Acceptance stops the response clock; completion stops the repair clock. Reopening retains the original deadlines.</value></data>
<data name="PartsAllocationHelp" xml:space="preserve"><value>Reserve stock, issue it to a work location, then consume it or return unused parts to the source. Reserved and issued balances cannot be used by other orders. Controlled stock still needs an independent witness. Only consumption is charged as a parts expense.</value></data>
<data name="OperationsAnalyticsHelp" xml:space="preserve"><value>Active time is time in progress; waiting includes requests, acceptance, assignment and holds. Downtime is the union of safety holds per order. Missing status history stays unknown. Preventive compliance uses original due dates, including overdue unfinished work. Repeated failures share an asset or unit and a recorded cause.</value></data>
